{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nDuring the comment-remediation Group17 full `make verify` run on macOS/Git 2.56, `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py::test_write_survives_foreground_maintenance_repack` failed because the ticket-create `git commit` exceeded its monkeypatched `_GIT_TIMEOUT=1.0`. The same unchanged test passed in 163.96 seconds isolated and again in 44.00 seconds with Git Trace2 under concurrent suites; the latter measured both ticket-create commits at 0.015 seconds each. The Group17 patch changes only comments in other files and preserves normalized AST. At the check, host load averages were 18.13/21.83/22.56, but the failed run has no Git trace, so the cause is unproven.\n\n## Measurements (2026-10-25, this host, real git, same 20,000-loose-object fixture)\n- The bounded `git commit` took 0.025 s and 0.019 s at host load 8 to 13; the explicit separate maintenance step took 6.5 s on its first run and 0.015 s on the second (its bound is 120 s). So the 1.0 s kill bound has about 40x headroom on a healthy commit.\n- A git shim that sleeps 1.3 s before `commit` (no repack involved) fails the test with exactly the reported \"git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out after 1.0s\". Any commit slower than 1 s fails it, whatever it is doing.\n- Git Trace2 (`GIT_TRACE2_EVENT`) shows the real structural difference. With the suppression in place, no `maintenance`, `gc` or `repack` process is a descendant of the `git commit` process; the explicit step is a separate top-level `git maintenance run --auto` and owns the repack. With the original defect (`_AUTOMAINT_OFF` emptied), `git maintenance run --auto` is a CHILD of `git commit`, and `repack`, `pack-objects` and `multi-pack-index` hang below it. A flat search for any repack is wrong: the fixed flow also runs them, under the separate step.\n\n## Root cause\nThe test uses a wall-clock kill bound (1.0 s) as a proxy for the invariant \"auto-maintenance does not run inside the bounded commit\". The bound is valid only while a healthy commit stays under it; host starvation can break that without any maintenance running. Not reproduced: the original single failure under load (the failed run had no Git trace), so the exact slow step there is unknown.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py`, stop patching `_GIT_TIMEOUT` to 1.0 and keep the production 30 s default.\n2. Set `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` to a file via `monkeypatch.setenv` and run the two creates.\n3. Parse the trace with a helper: collect the sids of top-level `commit` processes (a sid with no `/`, argv containing `commit`), then report every process whose sid starts with one of those sids plus `/` and whose command is `maintenance`, `gc`, `repack`, `pack-objects` or `multi-pack-index`.\n4. Assert at least one `commit` process was traced (so an empty trace cannot pass), that no maintenance descendant exists, and that both creates return ids.\n5. Add a detector test with the suppression removed (`event_commit_git._AUTOMAINT_OFF` set to `()`): the same helper must now find a maintenance descendant of a commit. This replaces the proof the 1 s bound used to give.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py`. Out of scope: production code, `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, the explicit maintenance step, and its 120 s bound.\n\n## Testing\n```\npytest tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py -q\nmake verify\n```\nAlso run the new test with a git shim that sleeps 1.3 s before `commit` (it must still pass, since no kill bound is involved). Failure case: with `_AUTOMAINT_OFF` emptied the new maintenance-descendant assertion fails, deterministically, with no dependence on timing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test fails when the suppression is removed and passes with it, without relying on a wall-clock bound (checked: detector test, and a seeded run with `_AUTOMAINT_OFF` emptied).\n- [ ] The test passes when every `git commit` is delayed 1.3 s (checked: shim run recorded in a ticket comment).\n- [ ] The commit-maintenance invariant is still asserted: no maintenance, gc or repack descendant of a commit (checked: the test body).\n- [ ] `make verify` is green on the Linux CI gate (`Verified +1` on the Gerrit change).\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792935093801406001,"uuid":"dfee6dfd-be6c-4f4d-8487-6b8fcd030124"}